    "short_description": "PetroChina Company Limited is a leading Chinese state-owned oil and gas enterprise, established on November 5, 1999. It operates as the listed arm of the China National Petroleum Corporation (CNPC) and is recognized as China's largest oil and gas producer and distributor. Headquartered in Beijing, PetroChina has a significant presence in both domestic and international markets, with a market capitalization of approximately $130 billion as of 2023.\n\nThe company engages in a wide range of activities across the oil and gas value chain, including exploration, production, refining, and marketing. PetroChina is the largest oil producer in China, contributing around 50% of the country's oil and 60% of its natural gas. It also has a robust international trading operation, focusing on global commodities and energy projects. The company emphasizes innovation, environmental stewardship, and energy security, aiming to transform into a competitive international energy firm while supporting China's energy needs.",
